    <section class="prose-section" style="margin-top: 0;">
        <h2 class="author-section-title">Background &amp; Mathematical Expertise</h2>
        <p>Born on July 14, 1998, Ervin Džakmić developed a deep passion for mathematics, quantitative analysis, and logic at an early age. His academic and personal fascination with mathematical formulas naturally evolved into a career spent designing high-impact software, optimizing digital products, and building user-centric SaaS platforms.</p>
        <p>Throughout his professional career, Ervin has worked as a Product Manager, Salesman, Digital Marketer, and SaaS Strategist. Combining data-driven growth strategies with mathematical precision, he specializes in building lean, accessible software solutions that bridge the gap between complex algorithms and effortless user experiences.</p>

        <h2 class="author-section-title">Why QuixCalc Was Built</h2>
        <p>The web is full of online calculator tools, but many of them present significant usability and privacy drawbacks. Users are frequently subjected to intrusive pop-up ads, mandatory account creation, hidden paywalls, or slow server response times that upload sensitive personal inputs to unknown third-party databases.</p>
        <p>Recognizing these friction points, Ervin created <strong>QuixCalc</strong> with a straightforward mission: to provide the fastest, cleanest, and most reliable browser-based calculators on the internet.</p>

        <h2 class="author-section-title">Our Technical &amp; Privacy Guarantees</h2>
        <ul style="padding-left: 1.25rem; color: var(--text-sub); font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.8;">
            <li><strong>100% Client-Side Computation:</strong> Every calculation (from financial amortization to cryptographic UUID generation) processes locally inside your web browser. No calculation data is transmitted or stored on external servers.</li>
            <li><strong>Zero Mandatory Logins:</strong> Instant access to every utility without sign-up forms, email gates, or paywalls.</li>
            <li><strong>Mathematical Integrity:</strong> Formulas are verified against industry standards (including Mifflin-St Jeor for metabolic rates, standard financial formulas, and standard deviation algorithms).</li>
        </ul>

